WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.270 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  the former president and current vice  president of argentina christina  fernandez de kirchner is on trial in the  case that's dividing the nation  the prosecution says she led one of the  biggest corruption syndicates in the  country's history she calls it a  political witch hunt  this trial started with this fiction  that was recounted by the prosecutors  over five days during those five days i  listened to those accusations that were  not accusations they were a fiction a  script a very bad one besides being  false  the prosecution is calling for a 12-year  prison sentence and a lifetime ban on  the vice president holding public office  one opposition politician even demanded  her execution  in response her supporters took to the  streets outside her apartment in buenos  aires police controlled by the  opposition-led city government responded  aggressively provoking strong criticism  from the national government including  the president alberto fernandez  her supporters now keep a daily vigil  outside her home  when you put one of our main political  leaders on trial in such a weak case you  undermine democracy and a lot of blood  has been spilt to win our democracy  she did so much the school the city  metro gave food to the poor equip the  universities and gave a wish to  housewives  christina fernandez de kitchener divides  opinion like no other but this trial is  about much more than whether she's  guilty or not guilty it's about how many  argentines see the future of their  troubled country  a former president the wife of a former  president and now argentina's vice  president mrs kirchner has been around  for long enough to have made plenty of  friends and a lot of enemies  her opponents view the former president  as symbolic of the corruption that's  blighted argentina for generations they  want to prevent her standing again for  president in next year's elections  it will be historic for argentina the  first time a female president convicted  for a fully proven corruption crime let  it serve as an example for all  it gives us hope that we still have  justice in argentina and this has only  just begun  the verdict on christina kitchner and  the 12 other accused is expected later  this year whatever the outcome argentina  will be divided by an increasingly  bitter conflict  daniel schweiner al jazeera buenos aires

